---

<ServicePage
  path="/services/managed-it"
  title="Managed IT & Support"
  description="Managed IT for small businesses in the Central Valley: remote management, verified off-site backups, phones, email and planning, from one team that knows your setup."
  intro="Remote management, backups verified before they leave the building, phones, email and planning. One team that already knows your setup, and picks up when you call."
  capabilities={capabilities}
  serviceTypes={["Managed IT Services", "Remote IT Support", "Data Backup and Recovery"]}
  examples={examples}
  quoteService="Managed IT & Support"
  ctaTitle="Want someone already watching?"
  ctaText="Tell us what you run and what keeps you up at night. The assessment is free."
>
  <p>
    A backup nobody has checked is a hope, not a backup. Every one we take is checksummed and
    verified before it leaves the building, the off-site copy lives on hardware we run, and we
    get an alert when one fails to arrive &mdash; so nobody learns a backup is missing on the
    day it&apos;s needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    The same goes for the rest of it. We set up remote management on every machine, keep
    everything patched, and write down what&apos;s where. When you call, you reach someone who
    already knows your setup, not a ticket queue.
  </p>
</ServicePage>
